---
title: Pumpkin Cheesecake Bars
description: Pumpkin cheesecake bars on a ginger graham crust, with the puree cooked down on the stove first.
tags: [bars, baking, fall]
course: dessert
icons: [pumpkin, cheese, pie]
source:
  name: Cook's Illustrated
  url: https://www.americastestkitchen.com/recipes/8182-pumpkin-cheesecake-bars
yield: 24%bars
time: 8h30m
---

= Pumpkin

Combine the @unsweetened pumpkin puree{1%can}(15 oz), @pumpkin pie spice{2%tsp}, and @salt{1/2%tsp} in a #small saucepan{}. Cook the mixture, stirring constantly, over medium heat until reduced to 1 1/2 cups, ~reduce{6-8%minutes}. Let the mixture cool for ~cool{1%hour}.

= Crust

Adjust the oven rack to the middle position and heat the oven to 325°F (165°C). Make a foil sling for a 13-by-9-inch #baking pan{}. Grease the #aluminum foil{}.

Process the @graham crackers{15}(whole, broken into 1-inch pieces), @sugar{50%g}(1/4 cup), and @ground ginger{1%tsp} in a #food processor{} to fine crumbs, about ~process{15%seconds}.

Add the @butter{112%g}(8 tbsp, melted) and pulse until combined, about 5 pulses.

Sprinkle the mixture into the prepared pan and press into an even layer. Bake until just starting to brown, ~bake{15-18%minutes}. Let the crust cool completely on a #wire rack{}.

= Filling

Using a #stand mixer{} fitted with the paddle, beat the @cream cheese{1%lb}(454 g, softened) and the remaining @&sugar{265%g} on medium-low speed until smooth, about ~beat{2%minutes}. Add the @lemon juice{1%tbsp}, @vanilla extract{2%tsp}, and pumpkin mixture and beat until combined. Increase the speed to medium; add the @eggs{4}(large, room temperature), one at a time; and beat until incorporated.

Pour over the cooled crust and spread into an even layer. Bake until the edges are slightly puffed and the center is just set, ~bake{45-50%minutes}.

= Chill

Let the cheesecake cool in the pan on the wire rack for ~cool{2%hours}.

Cover the pan with #plastic wrap{} and refrigerate the cheesecake for at least ~chill{3%hours} or up to 24 hours.

Using the foil overhang, lift the cheesecake out of the pan. Cut into 24 pieces before serving.
